Subject: [PATCH] docs: add fork policy, PC roadmap and language baselines

AGENTS_PROJECT.md records the authority order (project > baselines > upstream
policy), the release-tag sync policy, the version scheme and every deviation
this fork takes from the two generic baselines.

PRD.md v0.9 is the product fact source: data contract, prompt assembly order,
notes taxonomy, remote-mode auth and delivery shape. TODO.md tracks the 17
PC-side items together with the code fact each one was checked against, so
nothing in it rests on an assumption about the upstream tree.

AGENTS.md keeps a 300-character pointer section instead of inlining 120k of
baseline prose: the root file is capped at 12,000 chars and the loader chain
truncates at 30,000, so inlining would have silently dropped most of it.
